Subject: target/i386: restrict kernel nested-state validation to KVM

TCG SVM has architectural guest-mode state, but does not use KVM's opaque
nested-state blob. Keep the consistency check for the KVM accelerator.
QEMU 10.2.1 already serializes TCG SVM NPT and interrupt-control state.

--- a/target/i386/machine.c
+++ b/target/i386/machine.c
@@ -355,7 +355,7 @@
     env->hflags |= (env->segs[R_SS].flags >> DESC_DPL_SHIFT) & HF_CPL_MASK;
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_KVM
-    if ((env->hflags & HF_GUEST_MASK) &&
+    if (kvm_enabled() && (env->hflags & HF_GUEST_MASK) &&
         (!env->nested_state ||
         !(env->nested_state->flags & KVM_STATE_NESTED_GUEST_MODE))) {
         error_report("vCPU set in guest-mode inconsistent with "
